WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:05.790
Animal Planet's Call of the Wildman followed
the mostly toothless, bowie-knife-toting "Turtleman"

00:00:05.790 --> 00:00:10.630
Ernie Brown Jr. around the backwoods of Kentucky
as he responded to calls from people needing

00:00:10.630 --> 00:00:12.080
help with dangerous pests.

00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:16.640
His unique style of catching dangerous prey,
usually with his bare hands, quickly grew

00:00:16.650 --> 00:00:21.099
a rabid fanbase, but the show abruptly stopped
after its fourth season.

00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:22.060
So what happened?

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:24.560
This is the untold truth of the Turtleman.

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:26.640
Hungry for turtles

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:31.980
Ernie "Turtleman" Brown Jr.'s hardscrabble
lifestyle is all he's ever known, according

00:00:31.990 --> 00:00:34.190
to an interview with Channel Guide Magazine.

00:00:34.190 --> 00:00:37.880
Brown told the publication that he got his
nickname at the age of 7, saying,

00:00:37.880 --> 00:00:42.470
"We ran out of food one day, and my uncle
came over and took me and my dad to these

00:00:42.470 --> 00:00:46.850
old farm ponds, and he goes, 'I'll show you
how to get some meat on the table.'

00:00:46.850 --> 00:00:50.140
So he went out in that pond and turtles started
bubbling up."

00:00:50.540 --> 00:00:52.300
Shredder's got nothing on this guy.

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:54.420
Nothing but the tooth

00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:57.860
Aside from his giant knife and wildman yelp…

00:00:58.320 --> 00:00:59.020
"(yelling)"

00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:02.360
...the Turtleman is also known for his dental
deficiencies.

00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:07.400
Most people start correcting their oral hygiene
the second they make any TV money, but not

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:07.900
Turtleman.

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:12.540
Speaking with Syracuse.com, Turtleman laid
out the three incidents that left him with

00:01:12.549 --> 00:01:14.130
just seven teeth, saying,

00:01:14.130 --> 00:01:19.549
"The first one, a guy swung a chainsaw around
and hit me in the face while we clearing some

00:01:19.549 --> 00:01:20.049
brush.

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:22.880
That took 189 stitches to sew me back up."

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:23.900
Next?

00:01:24.340 --> 00:01:29.560
Turtleman lost a few more teeth in a car accident
when he tried to, quote, "Dukes of Hazzard"

00:01:29.580 --> 00:01:31.560
it over a ditch to avoid a tractor.

00:01:31.820 --> 00:01:33.700
And the third attack on his chompers?

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:36.620
He was whacked by a piece of metal during
a roofing job.

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:42.060
On top of being a crazy person who grabs wild
animals with his bare hands, this guy is also

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:45.900
apparently a walking installment of the Final
Destination movie franchise.

00:01:46.260 --> 00:01:51.300
In addition to those injuries, he's been bitten
at least 33 times by turtles.

00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:54.909
At least once, he nearly bled to death after
being bitten on the wrist.

00:01:54.909 --> 00:02:01.200
In a separate attack, a turtle got a mouthful
of Ernie Brown Jr.'s, um, little Turtleman.

00:02:01.940 --> 00:02:02.920
Animal abuse

00:02:03.420 --> 00:02:08.660
After a seven-month investigation into Call
of the Wildman, Mother Jones revealed not

00:02:08.670 --> 00:02:13.850
only the shady staging of the "rescues" on
the show, but also some serious allegations

00:02:13.850 --> 00:02:15.400
of animal abuse and neglect.

00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:19.890
Citing multiple examples of alleged animal
mismanagement, Mother Jones suggests the production

00:02:19.890 --> 00:02:24.980
team was complicit in illegally drugging animals
and failing to properly document wildlife

00:02:24.980 --> 00:02:26.560
activities for Kentucky officials.

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:32.480
In one incident, the crew sedated a zebra
which was procured from a local drive-thru

00:02:32.489 --> 00:02:35.599
animal safari, which Turtleman then "caught."

00:02:35.599 --> 00:02:40.599
In another, Turtleman cleared bats from an
area that were intentionally placed there.

00:02:40.599 --> 00:02:45.600
His activities resulted in the death of one
bat, and possibly violated local laws that

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:50.500
prevent "bringing a bat to a new location
for entertainment purposes alone."

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:56.240
Which is a very weird law to have to specify,
but hey, things get weird when you're bored.

00:02:56.920 --> 00:03:01.459
After the initial Mother Jones exposé, which
was published between seasons three and four

00:03:01.460 --> 00:03:05.720
of the show, Call of the Wildman saw a 43%
drop in ratings.

00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:10.920
Although there was never an official cancellation
announcement from Animal Planet, the Turtleman

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:13.260
never returned after that dismal fourth season.

00:03:14.140 --> 00:03:15.540
Not-so-live action

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:22.140
Despite well-documented instances of faking
genuine animal captures, Turtleman insists

00:03:22.140 --> 00:03:24.939
that he's the real deal, telling Channel Guide
Magazine,

00:03:24.939 --> 00:03:28.689
"People have been calling me fake, and there
ain't no fake.

00:03:28.689 --> 00:03:30.250
Go ahead and try it!

00:03:30.250 --> 00:03:32.250
We're doing it live action.

00:03:32.250 --> 00:03:33.930
We're there, doing our thing.

00:03:33.930 --> 00:03:36.360
I'm catching animals, that's the way it is."

00:03:36.920 --> 00:03:42.240
But while The Turtleman may be endearingly
genuine, his TV show was not.

00:03:42.250 --> 00:03:45.720
Animal Planet is remarkably open about this
fact.

00:03:45.720 --> 00:03:50.909
Animal Planet's Senior VP of Communications
Patricia Kollappallil, addressed an episode

00:03:50.909 --> 00:03:56.469
in which, quote, "a poisonous non-native snake
was released into a city swimming pool without

00:03:56.469 --> 00:04:01.549
proper authorization," by shifting blame to
the show's producers, saying,

00:04:01.549 --> 00:04:06.560
"We're clear we do dramatizations, so for
us that wasn't news or controversial.

00:04:06.560 --> 00:04:08.930
Sharp [Entertainment] did bring in snakes."

00:04:08.930 --> 00:04:12.690
"There are times for a story line we need
a particular animal, and we'll work with a

00:04:12.690 --> 00:04:14.780
licenser to find the particular animal."

00:04:15.020 --> 00:04:18.459
A show producer who spoke to Mother Jones
confirmed the trickery.

00:04:18.459 --> 00:04:22.840
"It was part of my job to call around people
to trap animals at the direction of Sharp.

00:04:22.840 --> 00:04:24.020
It's 100 percent fake."

00:04:24.640 --> 00:04:25.560
Lost license

00:04:26.480 --> 00:04:29.100
One thing about the Turtleman was definitely
real.

00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:35.080
For a time, Ernie Brown Jr. was a licensed
Nuisance Wildlife Control Officer in the commonwealth

00:04:35.080 --> 00:04:35.640
of Kentucky.

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:38.780
That is, until he stepped out of bounds on
TV.

00:04:38.990 --> 00:04:45.080
In 2013, Turtleman was hit with a violation
of his NWCO license after an episode in which

00:04:45.080 --> 00:04:50.720
he wrangled a deer out of a store in exchange
for "an authentic suit of armor."

00:04:51.040 --> 00:04:56.760
One problem: deer did not fall under his jurisdiction
as a nuisance officer, so the commonwealth

00:04:56.760 --> 00:05:01.940
of Kentucky issued him a friendly reminder
that if he was ever shown to mess with elk,

00:05:01.940 --> 00:05:07.300
deer, wild turkey, or bear again, he could
lose his license for three years, and possibly

00:05:07.300 --> 00:05:08.520
receive a criminal citation.

00:05:09.180 --> 00:05:14.610
Shortly after, inconsistencies were found
in Turtleman's NWCO paperwork, and several

00:05:14.610 --> 00:05:19.380
agencies, including the USDA and The Humane
Society called for the cancellation of the

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:20.120
show.

00:05:20.240 --> 00:05:24.420
The Kentucky Department of Fish and Wildlife
also confirmed to Mother Jones that Turtleman

00:05:24.430 --> 00:05:29.410
was no longer licensed in the state as a nuisance
officer, and though they wouldn't say why,

00:05:29.410 --> 00:05:30.300
the answer is pretty obvious.

00:05:31.460 --> 00:05:32.680
Turtleman Strong

00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:38.080
Along with country artist Steve Oliver, Turtleman
is in the process of putting together a series

00:05:38.080 --> 00:05:40.080
of albums that will tell the story of his
life.

00:05:40.580 --> 00:05:45.360
True to his word, he recently dropped his
first music video, "Turtleman Strong."

00:05:45.360 --> 00:05:50.759
It's an ambitious undertaking for the Turtleman
to say the least; he and Oliver have written

00:05:50.760 --> 00:05:54.120
90 songs that they plan on turning into three
albums.

00:05:54.900 --> 00:05:56.199
"Ya'll ain't seen nothin' yet.

00:05:56.200 --> 00:05:58.240
Turtleman's comin' back 2017.

00:05:58.960 --> 00:05:59.960
Turtleman strong."

00:06:00.240 --> 00:06:04.520
And with the recent appearance of Turtleman's
own official YouTube channel, could this be

00:06:04.520 --> 00:06:07.599
the resurgence of The Turtleman we've all
been waiting for?

00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:12.620
"If you subscribe to the channel, you'll never
miss… any live action (yelling)."

00:06:13.300 --> 00:06:14.220
Thanks for watching!

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:17.160
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:06:17.169 --> 00:06:19.350
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

